nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T05:27:18-07:00","id":1513635,"title":"","content":"Interesting idea with a lot of potential. But what I'd really like is some rpgs for my rpg setting","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T05:36:09-07:00","id":1513636,"title":"","content":"Mmmm... I'm just full of negativity on this one.<ul><li>Game set in Venice; protagonist is apparently an <i>Assamite</i> instead of the other obvious choice of my favourite clan.</li> <li>Assamite protagonist somehow has Oblivion [Obtenebration]</li> </ul>These are, of course, entirely personal gripes and come down to preference, but I would pass this up on that alone. And, even if I was inclined to play, why VR. <i>Why</i>. Could we not have non-VR alternatives? Even if I could afford one, I get horrific motion sickness that makes me unable to use it. (I'm still so mad that the only Wraith game in existence is barred to me)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T13:08:56-07:00","id":1513691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513634-new-v-tm-video-game-announced?p=1513635#post1513635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting idea with a lot of potential. But what I'd really like is some rpgs for my rpg setting</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, me too. Even if I don't play some video games (not only WoD based but generally speaking) I still like to use certain parts of the plot/setting during my games. That's why when my players listen to the radio I mix my playlist with radio commercials from GTA series <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. And that's why I would like somebody to create a plot description based on quests from V:tM Bloodhunt. Even if I don't like a battle royale games I think I would be able to create a decent story based on Bloodhunt. So if any of you guys could do it for me I would be grateful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"