:"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T23:35:31-07:00","id":1513747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513634-new-v-tm-video-game-announced?p=1513698#post1513698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> V5's character creation allows the pick of two of three clan disciplines. The protagonist's disciplines are Blood Sorcery and Obfuscate, drinks from vampires as well as mortals, the theme is &quot;Justice&quot;; Assamite is the most obvious conclusion.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you say so. I have to admit that I'm not very familiar with 5th edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T23:37:04-07:00","id":1513748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513634-new-v-tm-video-game-announced?p=1513720#post1513720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Several articles have revealed that the PC is a Banu Haqim traveling from New York to Venice to find her Sire's killer.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>So you dug deeper than I.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-03T01:15:26-07:00","id":1513751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513634-new-v-tm-video-game-announced?p=1513735#post1513735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another Vampoire: the Masquerade role-playing and adventure video game. VtM : Bloodlines 2 is certainly making a good enough impression, but the setting, the metaplot, and the storyline of VtM could definitely use another WoD video or computer game. I tthink that it is clear that in regard to VtM ( and also WoD - for example MtA ) computer games of the grand strategy, empire building, and nation managment type would be complex, worthwhile, and intricate.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I actually think this would be a really good idea from Paradox since it actually plays to their stengths instead of chasing flavour of the week like vr and battle royales.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-03T02:34:00-07:00","id":1513755,"title":"","content":"I actually like the idea of an Assamite cleaning up Venice, except y'know, Assamites who do this kind of thing are extremists, and the writing makes it sound heroic. <br /> <br /> I'm also bothered by this bit here. <br /> Hide from the guilty in plain sight with Cloak of Shadows, boil the insides of your victims with Cauldron of Blood, or place a Shadow Trap to drag them into Oblivion. Drink the blood of mortals and other vampires to keep your Hunger at bay. The crossbow attached to your arm can be used for both puzzle solving and combat.<br /> <br /> 1: As much as I love Deus Ex and It'd be really awesome if this was the vibe they were going for, a wrist crossbow is a stupid weapon. <br /> 2: <i>Hunger</i>. Give me the Beast or give me death. <br /> 3: Oblivion? No; No, No, No. No No Na na na na na na.. Joan Crawford has risen from the grave. <br /> 4: Why would a celerity using assamite be excited about Cauldron of blood? <br /> 5: a stealth game where the player is going to have obfuscate means that obfuscate is probably going to be done very strangely (like, I can imagine a good stealth game where obfuscate is done as in V20 because there's lots of circumstances where obfuscate would fail but.. anyhow. <br /> 6: Celerity IS a combat discipline though, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-03T03:27:57-07:00","id":1513757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513634-new-v-tm-video-game-announced?p=1513755#post1513755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">6: Celerity IS a combat discipline though, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>@<b><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth\">Rhywbeth</a></b>\u200b suggested earlier in the thread that the player character's powers just follow V5 character creation where you pick two out of the three clan disciplines; in this case, Obfuscate and <s>Thaumaturgy</s> Blood Sorcery. Also, the developers might not want to deal with super-speed as a player tool, especially in VR.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-03T03:28:00-07:00","id":1513758,"title":"","content":"On the downside I have no hopes or expectations. But on the plus side since it's a VR game and I don't own a VR device, I won't ever be able to play it so I don't have to worry about being disappointed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-03T03:50:41-07:00","id":1513759,"title":"","content":"Why not just do a Dishonored like game without VR? Or even better, do what Pathfinder did with Kingmaker and Wrath of the Righteous and give us a proper game?<br /> At least this couldn't be worse than Bloodlines 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-03T05:33:46-07:00","id":1513761,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1190_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1190\" data-vbnamecard=\"1190\">Elphilm</a> <br /> <br /> Bloodlines, for all it's butchery of Animalism, did celerity really well, and genuinely while video games struggle with something abstract like Dominate or Animalism, Celerity is something purely mathematical and that's easier to simulate in a game than it is in table top where the simplicity of human-rolled dice limits you.<br /> <br /> You just slow everything down while your character stays at the same speed, or you speed things up. You can map it to a button. FEAR's whole shtick was using slow-mo for mayhem, BroForce has one time-slowing guy that has a whole level dedicated to him speeding through an exploding facility.<b> Superhot's VR version sold more than the original game</b>. There's Max Payne, there's a whole bunch of titles with the word Time in them... <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-03T07:58:51-07:00","id":1513772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513634-new-v-tm-video-game-announced?p=1513739#post1513739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The available descriptions, drawings, trailers, and pictures from V : tM Bloodlines 2 do give a normal, reasonable, and distinct idea that this game is being made with anattention to the story, the setting, variety, and gameplay quality. This type of effort and work does make sense - great expectations come with VtM : Bloodlines 2 being a definite progression from VtM : Bloodlines 1.<br /> <br /> I have to mention that of course there are a few wonderous, great, good, and normal card games based on the World of Darkness and Vampire : the Masquerade.<br /> These card systems are simply and definitely a perfect setting and story expansion and development, for WoD and V : tM , while at the same time being good entertainment and positive intellectual challange.</div> </div> </div> </div>My English is not perfect, but what it seems is that first you commented that bloodline 2 is being done carelessly and then that this is to be expected considering that it is a sequel to the first game. Did I understand correctly or was there a translation problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-03T08:51:21-07:00","id":1513778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513634-new-v-tm-video-game-announced?p=1513761#post1513761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You just slow everything down while your character stays at the same speed, or you speed things up. You can map it to a button. FEAR's whole shtick was using slow-mo for mayhem, BroForce has one time-slowing guy that has a whole level dedicated to him speeding through an exploding facility.<b> Superhot's VR version sold more than the original game</b>. There's Max Payne, there's a whole bunch of titles with the word Time in them...</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, I wasn't saying that super-speed is difficult to implement in general. We've all seen a bunch of games with that as the central gimmick. I was simply thinking out loud that <i>these</i> developers might not want to deal with it for <i>this</i> particular project. It's a first-person game, and there might simply be issues that have yet to be ironed out with slowing/speeding up a first-person VR experience and player disorientation. I wouldn't know, I've never even played a VR game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-03T12:13:21-07:00","id":1513799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513634-new-v-tm-video-game-announced?p=1513751#post1513751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I actually think this would be a really good idea from Paradox since it actually plays to their stengths instead of chasing flavour of the week like vr and battle royales.</div> </div> </div> </div>EXACTLY!<br /> <br /> Like seriously, WTF is Paradox doing??<br /> <br /> They have the whole WoD franchise in their grip and they HAVEN'T made a grand strategy game out of any of the splats? Why do they keep allowing these outside affiliated studios make these dumb VR and Battle Royale games that keep flopping? <br /> <br /> Sure, you can play either the CK2 or CK3 Prince of Darkness mods to play in a grand strategy WoD setting.. but it's not the same as fully realized standalone game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-03T13:50:17-07:00","id":1513810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513634-new-v-tm-video-game-announced?p=1513799#post1513799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> EXACTLY!<br /> <br /> Like seriously, WTF is Paradox doing??<br /> <br /> They have the whole WoD franchise in their grip and they HAVEN'T made a grand strategy game out of any of the splats? Why do they keep allowing these outside affiliated studios make these dumb VR and Battle Royale games that keep flopping?<br /> <br /> Sure, you can play either the CK2 or CK3 Prince of Darkness mods to play in a grand strategy WoD setting.. but it's not the same as fully realized standalone game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe they wanted to expand and earn more so they went with what was most popular or what they think is popular.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-03T16:45:37-07:00","id":1513827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513634-new-v-tm-video-game-announced?p=1513799#post1513799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> EXACTLY!<br /> <br /> Like seriously, WTF is Paradox doing??<br /> <br /> They have the whole WoD franchise in their grip and they HAVEN'T made a grand strategy game out of any of the splats? Why do they keep allowing these outside affiliated studios make these dumb VR and Battle Royale games that keep flopping?<br /> <br /> Sure, you can play either the CK2 or CK3 Prince of Darkness mods to play in a grand strategy WoD setting.. but it's not the same as fully realized standalone game.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, they haven\u2019t made any video games from the IP period. Everything released to date has been done by someone licensing the WoD IP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-04T02:53:38-07:00","id":1513852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513634-new-v-tm-video-game-announced?p=1513799#post1513799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> EXACTLY!<br /> <br /> Like seriously, WTF is Paradox doing??<br /> <br /> They have the whole WoD franchise in their grip and they HAVEN'T made a grand strategy game out of any of the splats? Why do they keep allowing these outside affiliated studios make these dumb VR and Battle Royale games that keep flopping?<br /> <br /> Sure, you can play either the CK2 or CK3 Prince of Darkness mods to play in a grand strategy WoD setting.. but it's not the same as fully realized standalone game.</div> </div> </div> </div>My idea would be an xcom style campaign where you manage a city under assault from the Sabbat. You manage a number of coteries and would handle a number of variables- masquerade, territory, humanity of coteries, loyalty of primogen Council etc. You could do a lot with something like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 06-04-2023, 06:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-04T05:14:04-07:00","id":1513862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513634-new-v-tm-video-game-announced?p=1513852#post1513852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My idea would be an xcom style campaign where you manage a city under assault from the Sabbat. You manage a number of coteries and would handle a number of variables- masquerade, territory, humanity of coteries, loyalty of primogen Council etc. You could do a lot with something like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>A few years ago there was a thread during which we discussed our ideas for a perfect WoD game:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1152201-the-ideal-wod-video-game#post1177736\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1152201-the-ideal-wod-video-game#post1177736\"> The ideal WoD video game - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1152201-the-ideal-wod-video-game#post1177736\"> https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1152201-the-ideal-wod-video-game#post1177736 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> So... I've been thinking about how to create a good WoD game: it's not easy. As has been discussed on the forum before many of the disciplines are not what might </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> We even tried to assemble a team of creators to make our ideas a living thing but it died naturally. Maybe, as long as there is a World of Darkness Unbound project, we should try again. There are a few games already created by community and some of them are fairly good. Sadly I think that Paradox employees doesn't read our posts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-04T07:17:54-07:00","id":1513871,"title":"","content":"Many games adaptating the wod seems to only take a few elements of the ttrpgs, which of course is frustrating when we know that there are ways to creates video games matching the feeling of the originals.<br /> <br /> They should be rpgs of course, but not necessarily bloodlines-like action rpg. <br /> <br /> Personally, I think the best exemples to make perfect wod games would be top down rgs like divinity original sins, or baldur's gates. Such games would allow the feeling of playing an actual ttrpg (which was the goal of larian studio's devs).<br /> <br /> And for less action oriented games, like a political vampire games, or a wraith investigation one, you could always do a non action top down rpg like disco elysium.<br /> <br /> And the worse is that paradox already has those ideas... For tabletop games. Vampire chapters and werewolf retaliation are already halfway between the ttrpg and what a faithful video game could be.<br /> <br /> And vampire legacy is basically a tabletop version of what a crusader kings vampire game could be.<br /> <br /> So seriously paradox, you bought this pretty costy ip, when are you going to do what you know will be successfull and that you know how to do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-04T08:10:02-07:00","id":1513876,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I would also like a RPG game like Baldur's Gate. But I think that it would be best as W:tA game. Vampires are IMHO too attached to the cities so it would propably be more like Pool of Radiance. Plus a Vampire is too politically oriented. I think it would be better to create a grand strategy game (even if this grandeuse is limited to one city) or political simulation. Or maybe a game similar to V:tM Redemption but far less combat oriented. Instead it could lead the main character through the ages (the thing that was wasted in Redemption) just like in Transylvania or Giovanni Cronicles. As for werewolf if it wasn't for 5th edition it would be at least 4 different stories that could be used as source material/inspiration<br /> <br /> 1. War in the Amazon - it would be more tactical RPG than traditional but still.<br /> 2. Campaign idea from Rage across Russia and Revelations of Dark Mother - more like Baldur's Gate: the characters start as a Silver Pack sidekicks send to Russia to investigate Shadow Courtain. There the Silver Pack is slained and the characters have to deal with Baba Yaga. I run this story once and it was great<br /> 3. Campaign idea from Rage Across Australia where players are chosen by Greek Twice Tongue and send for various places to revive Rainbow Serpent. There could be also a hard mora\u0142 choice: to help Cernouros revive thelacines and Bunyip or not.<br /> 4. Samuel Height story. I know, many of players and storytellers hate it but I think that after some modifications it could be great: starting at Valkenburg Foundation then going to NY for a Sabbat clash. After that some action in Chicago during war with vampires. Later some more fighting in Amazon. And, for the last part, Crombey's farm, New Orlean and, in the end, Mexico.<br /> <br /> Sadly it looks that Paradox, just like Disney before, will throw away earlier editions.<br /> <br /> It could also be good for a Mage story (but I'm afraid that paradox rules could be hard to be implanted in video game). Changeling comes next, maybe even breaking the 4th wall. It could be an epic journey, with fights against the goblins and dragons, some courtly dialogue sections only to discover in the end that this was just some kind of a dream and the main character undergone Chrysalis. As for Wraith I would use a pararell stories, just like in Heartless Lullaby: one for Wraith and one for Orpheus operative (yeah, I know it's a little outdated but I'm still not very familiar with 20th Anniversary/5th editions).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-04T16:16:11-07:00","id":1513897,"title":"","content":"There could be another video game based on V:tM. For now it is called Project Cardinal (working title) by Draw Distance (Coteries of New York and Shadows of New York).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T02:33:16-07:00","id":1514177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513634-new-v-tm-video-game-announced?p=1513761#post1513761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1190_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1190\" data-vbnamecard=\"1190\">Elphilm</a><br /> Bloodlines, for all it's butchery of Animalism, did celerity really well, and genuinely while video games struggle with something abstract like Dominate or Animalism,<br /> <br /> (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if some qualities and traits of characters or abilities are given a lesser or less visible role, as long as these traits or abilities are respected as parrts and elements of the setting by being given at least some uniqueness and usefulness, then I consider that tthis section of design and portrayal of a particular role-playing game or book witihin a computer game ( or a card system, or a board game ) is done in a way that can certainly be considered positive and good enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-09T12:08:39-07:00","id":1514328,"title":"","content":"I accidentally stomped on an 2002 vampire (not Cainite) themed game called Erevos. It's a Myst like game but it have an interesting feature: it breaks the fourth wall by checking the time on your PC and allows you to play only between 8 PM and 7 AM. I have to admit that I played Bloodlines once like that (you know, in October, played a few hours every night, the rest I treated as travel time between different parts of LA) but I didn't know that someone would put in the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}